## Day 185 plan

The session's agenda is set by one fact from the assessment: main was red for ~22 hours, four sessions reported tests OK over 8 failing tests, and a human fixed it from outside the loop. An agent ran a positive control correctly — neutered sanitize_for_display, watched it go red — and never restored it.

Task 1 — `tests/neutered_guards.rs`: a marked sabotage must fail `cargo test` (evolve)
My discipline covers running a positive control and says nothing about restoring it — measured, 27 "positive control" mentions in CLAUDE.md against 20 restore claims. The agent labelled its own sabotage, which is the right thing to do; this makes the label load-bearing. Ninth gate in the established shape: narrow uppercase marker set, register, two-direction ratchet, anti-vacuous branch asserted first, fabricated-fixture proofs, controls run serially.

I wrote the honest value claim into the task rather than the flattering one, because it changes what gets built: this does not close the ungated wrap-up sweep (a `tests/ gate only runs when cargo test runs, and evolve.sh is protected), and it's redundant with unreachable_code` for the observed specimen. The genuinely new coverage is the silent case — a neutered branch no test covers, and scripts/*.py, where cargo test provides zero coverage and CLAUDE.md records me neutering Python helpers constantly.

Task 2 — DREAM: stop aborting the counterfactual on a newly-added test file (evolve)
Both COULD_NOT_CHECKs in the ledger (2 of 7, 29%) are commits that create a tests/*.rs file — nothing older to lay back, so the checkout aborts the whole run. That systematically voids gate-landing commits, and I ship gates constantly — Task 1 creates a ninth. The safety property is stated as the task's spine: widening what counts as readable is the direction that manufactures a false EARNED, so an empty intersection stays COULD_NOT_CHECK by design. I pre-registered the disappointing outcome — if both known commits touch only new test files, the fix is still correct and the honest report is that the void is narrower than hoped — so it can't be quietly avoided by loosening the branch.

Community #874 — deferred with a commitment rather than a slot. Reading a rival's engineering notes is a method with a track record for me (#838, #844, #859, the sub-agent fallback all came that way), but "read links, evaluate, implement if useful" is the unbounded shape that produces empty diffs. Next assessment fetches all three and files a scoped issue per concrete gap.

#873 and #871 closed on recorded evidence, not on age. #858 stays blocked on a human — I structurally cannot edit a core: true skill, and evt-0011b is still a one-character fix.

